PENROSE KITE AND DART — edge-typed enumeration at D=10
======================================================
Goal: every edge-to-edge PERIODIC tiling by Penrose's kite and dart, matched on edge LENGTH only
(the arrow decorations that force aperiodicity are directed and cannot be an undirected edge type).

Palette  tools/ctrnact-oracle/alphabets/palettes/penrose.json
  Kite  angles [72,72,144,72] = [2,2,4,2] at D=10   edges [phi,1,1,phi]
  Dart  angles [36,216,36,72] = [1,6,1,2] at D=10   edges [1,1,phi,phi]
  phi = 2cos(36) = zeta10 + zeta10^-1, already an algebraic integer in Z[zeta10] -> no length scaling.

Ring   develop_tri45.py generalised from hardcoded Z[zeta24] to Z[zeta_D] via render_ring.Ring(D).
  REGRESSION (2026-08-14): planigon k<=3 cells BYTE-IDENTICAL; tri45all/tri45sq/tri45two k<=4
  identical in geometry (11931 / 4919 / 2205 entries), differing only in the `id` prefix, which
  predates this change.

ALPHABET
  8 corner classes, 117 vertex configurations, 195 entries. A6 PASS (pairwise non-isomorphic).
  61 of 195 entries have sided classes — both tiles are achiral but sigma is non-trivial on each, which
  is exactly the hole the 2026-08-13 chirality-bit repair closed. Without it this palette would not run.

SEARCH
  k<=3 sequential (run-sts.sh penrose 3)   3 s      7 / 18 / 91
  k<=5 sequential (run-sts.sh penrose 5)   32 s     + 287 / 890
  k<=6 parallel, EU_SHARD_N=32 EU_SHARD_D2=8 EU_POOL=8   49 s wall, 37,525 raw blocks
       reproduces 7 / 18 / 91 / 287 / 890 EXACTLY, then k=6 = 3212. Total 4505.
  develop: 4505 of 4505, ZERO failures, 5.5 s.

CERTIFICATION (all 4505)
  every face is exactly a kite or a dart      113,467 faces, 0 anything else
  worst edge error vs {1, phi}                9.22e-10
  worst |sum face area - |det Lambda|| / cell 6.51e-10
  worst vertex turn error from 360 deg        2.59e-07   (reflex-safe: the dart's 216 deg counts as 216)
  independent coverage test: 4,640 random points in the period cell, each over a 5x5 lattice block,
  EVERY ONE covered by exactly one tile. No gaps, no overlaps. (A 3x3 block is too small — some faces
  reach past one lattice vector — which is what the first run's 94 "gaps" were.)

DEDUP
  4505 -> 4505. The pruner had already removed every congruent duplicate; the geometric pass merges
  nothing, up to rotation OR up to rotation and reflection. That number is only meaningful because the
  congruence oracle self-checks first: 41 entries rotated by a multiple of 36 deg, reflected and shifted
  off-lattice must come back congruent to themselves, and 41 cross-k pairs must not. The self-check
  CAUGHT A REAL BUG on its first run — the shape key sorted float coordinates, and a rotated copy of a
  symmetric face sorts its two equal-x vertices the other way round, so the oracle called tilings
  different from themselves and "0 duplicates" meant nothing.

EXPECTED TILINGS PRESENT (sanity, k=1)
  2 kites + 0 darts   the p2 rotation tiling of the kite (any quadrilateral tiles by 180 deg rotations
                      about its edge midpoints; Euler gives V = F, so 2 tiles and 2 vertices per cell)
  0 kites + 2 darts   the same for the dart, reflex corner and all
  1 kite  + 1 dart    the phi-rhombus, one of each, meeting at the valence-2 vertex where the dart's
                      216 deg notch is filled by the kite's 144 deg corner. min_len=2 is what admits it.

OPEN OBSERVATION — the kite/dart balance
  k       tilings    kites    darts
  1             7       15       15
  2            18       79       79
  3            91      617      617
  4           287     2466     2457
  5           890    10151    10151
  6          3212    43436    43384
  Exact at k = 1, 2, 3, 5 and broken at k = 4 and 6. At k<=3 the (kites, darts) profile pairs up
  perfectly too — (0,2)/(2,0), (1,3)/(3,1), (2,6)/(6,2), (4,12)/(12,4) all with matching multiplicity.
  I have no proof of a kite<->dart involution on the catalogue and the k=4/k=6 misses say any such map
  has exceptions. Recorded as an observation, NOT a claim.

SHELF
  4505 entries. k<=3 eager (294 KB); k=4/5/6 lazy (0.9 / 3.4 / 14.1 MB).
  /library and /play: Different edge lengths -> Palette -> Penrose kite and dart.
  NOTE the /play cost: KNOWN_HIGHER_TIERS is pulled eagerly on mount, so this adds 18.4 MB to that
  page's load, against the 19.5 MB the isotoxal k=4 shard already spends there.

FILL COLOUR (2026-08-14, AL request)
  The renderers colour a tile by its side count, drifted a little toward red by how far the outline is
  from regular. Kite and dart are both quadrilaterals, so both took polygonHue(4) = 45 deg and both
  drifted a few degrees — one flat orange field, with no way to see which tile was which. Each face now
  carries an explicit `hue`, the per-polygon override the renderers already honour for polyominoes
  (same problem there: one boundary side count, several pieces). Kite 45 deg, dart 205 deg. Verified on
  BOTH paths: the p5/canvas thumbnails on /library and the WebGL fill on /play.
